From ff32cfbaf72d06cf492b4a5f3049aaaebf56c06c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francisco Reyes <21211939+freyesperales@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:49:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs: fix install-without-curl_cffi instructions

requirements.txt was removed when dependencies moved to pyproject.toml,
so the documented curl command now gets a 404 and the following
`pip install --no-deps yfinance` leaves pandas, numpy and requests
uninstalled. Install normally and then remove curl_cffi; yfinance
already falls back to requests when curl_cffi is missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 doc/source/advanced/install.rst | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/source/advanced/install.rst b/doc/source/advanced/install.rst
index 320ddc9..59712c8 100644
--- a/doc/source/advanced/install.rst
+++ b/doc/source/advanced/install.rst
@@ -5,5 +5,5 @@ To install without ``curl_cffi`` for requests fallback:
 
 .. code-block:: bash
 
-    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ranaroussi/yfinance/main/requirements.txt | grep -vi '^curl_cffi' | pip install -r /dev/stdin
-    pip install --no-deps yfinance
+    pip install yfinance
+    pip uninstall -y curl_cffi
-- 
2.56.1.windows.1

